          <span class="std-badge">MN 7.1.4.4</span>
        </div>
        <div class="slide-body">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Surface Reading vs. Close Analysis:</strong> Reading for plot gets you started; reading for word choice and structure builds mastery.</li>
            <li><strong>Annotating Structure:</strong> Circle unknown roots, underline key arguments, and box structural transition markers.</li>
            <li><strong>Context Clues:</strong> Using surrounding paragraph logic to infer meanings of unfamiliar terms before checking a dictionary.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="callout-box">
          <strong style="color: var(--primary-dark);">📖 Active Reading:</strong> Good readers keep a pencil in hand to track morphological shifts across texts.
        </div>
      </div>

